  "id": "BIT-ghost-2026-105642",
  "summary": "Ghost: Remote Code Execution via Bookmark Card Images",
  "details": "Ghost is a Node.js content management system. From 6.56.0 until 6.67.0, an image processing library bundled with Ghost contained a vulnerability in its SVG handling. Any staff user, including Contributors, could create a bookmark card for an attacker-controlled website, resulting in arbitrary commands being run on the Ghost server. This issue is fixed in version 6.67.0.",
